NAME
     find - walk a directory tree, testing and acting on what is there

SYNOPSIS
     find [PATH...] [EXPRESSION]

DESCRIPTION
     find walks each PATH and evaluates EXPRESSION for everything it
     meets. With no expression it prints every name.

OPTIONS
     -name PAT, -iname PAT    the name matches (case-insensitively)
     -path PAT                the whole path matches
     -type f|d|l|b|c|p|s      the kind of thing it is
     -size N[ckMG]            its size
     -empty                   an empty file or directory
     -user NAME, -group NAME  its owner
     -perm MODE               its mode
     -links N                 its link count
     -inum N                  its inode number
     -mtime N, -mmin N        when it was last changed
     -newer FILE              changed more recently than FILE
     -maxdepth N, -mindepth N how deep to go
     -print, -print0, -ls     what to print
     -delete                  remove it
     -exec CMD {} ;           run CMD; -ok asks first
     -a, -o, -not, ( )        and, or, not, grouping
     -prune                   do not descend into this one

EXAMPLES
     find / -name '*.conf'
     find /tmp -type f -mtime +7 -delete
     find . -type f -print0 | xargs -0 wc -l

SEE ALSO
     xargs(1), ls(1), grep(1)
